{"book":40,"chapter":23,"context":{"chapter":23,"title":"Woes to the Hypocrites","summary":"Jesus warns the crowds against the example of the scribes and Pharisees, pronounces a series of woes on their hypocrisy, and laments over Jerusalem, which killed the prophets sent to it.","background":"The Pharisees were respected lay teachers devoted to keeping the law, and Jesus says they 'sit in Moses' seat' (v. 2). His criticism targets the gap between teaching and practice. 'Woe' is the prophets' language, part grief and part warning.","customs":[{"term":"Phylacteries and borders","verses":"23:5","note":"Phylacteries were small leather boxes holding Scripture, worn on arm and forehead (Deuteronomy 6:8); borders were garment tassels. Enlarging them drew attention."},{"term":"Whited sepulchres","verses":"23:27","note":"Touching a grave made a person ritually unclean (Numbers 19:16), so tombs were whitewashed to be seen and avoided."}],"watchFor":["The repeated cry 'Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites!'","Tithing tiny garden herbs while neglecting 'judgment, mercy, and faith' (v. 23).","Jesus' image of a hen gathering her chicks (v. 37)."],"connections":["Deuteronomy 6:8","Numbers 19:16","2 Chronicles 24:20-22","Psalms 118:26"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["Τότε","Tote","G5119","ADV","Then"],["ὁ","ho","G3588","T-NSM","<the>"],["Ἰησοῦς","Iēsous","G2424","N-NSM-P","Jesus"],["ἐλάλησεν","elalēsen","G2980","V-AAI-3S","spoke"],["τοῖς","tois","G3588","T-DPM","to the"],["ὄχλοις","ochlois","G3793","N-DPM","crowds"],["καὶ","kai","G2532","CONJ","and"],["τοῖς","tois","G3588","T-DPM","to the"],["μαθηταῖς","mathētais","G3101","N-DPM","disciples"],["αὐτοῦ","autou","G846","P-GSM","of Him"]],"x":[[40015010,40015020,4],[42012001,42012001,4],[42020045,42020046,4],[42012057,42012057,3]],"xn":4},"2":{"w":[["λέγων·","legōn","G3004","V-PAP-NSM","saying"],["ἐπὶ","epi","G1909","PREP","On"],["τῆς","tēs","G3588","T-GSF","<the>"],["Μωϋσέως","Mōuseōs","G3475","N-GSM-P","Moses’"],["καθέδρας","kathe